 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Rules are recorded as deferred callbacks on the bundle, then replayed against the app at registration.\n\n- **`Bundle.attach_route_rule`** (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:413`): when you declare a route, it does not touch the app. It validates the names and calls `self.record(lambda s: s.attach_route_rule(...))` (L433).\n  - **`Bundle.record`** (L224) appends that lambda to `self.deferred_functions`.\n- **`Tessel.register_bundle`** (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:571`) calls **`Bundle.register(app, options)`** (`bundles.py:273`).\n  - `Bundle.register` creates a **`BundleSetupState`** (via `make_setup_state`, L246). The state holds the app, the options, the URL prefix, the subdomain and the name prefix.\n  - It then replays the deferred callbacks with `for deferred in self.deferred_functions: deferred(state)` (L334).\n- **`BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule`** (`bundles.py:87`) does the actual attaching:\n  - It prepends `url_prefix` to the rule, and sets the subdomain and merged `url_defaults`.\n  - It prefixes the endpoint as `<name_prefix>.<bundle name>.<endpoint>`.\n  - It calls **`app.attach_route_rule(...)`** (`sansio/app.py:606`), which adds the rule to the app's URL map.",
